const judgments={
 ALE:['Expected annual loss uses SLE multiplied by annual expected frequency.','Model estimate, not guaranteed loss or a probability; currency/event times events/year. Fractional ARO is valid; uncertainty, dependencies and loss distribution are not taught here.'],
 ARO:['Estimated number of occurrences in one year.','Frequency may be below or above one; not a percentage, probability or proof of future incidents. Exposure interval and model assumptions must match.'],
 SLE:['Expected loss associated with one risk occurrence.','Single-event money differs from annual loss and occurrence frequency. The conventional AV times fractional EF model is contextual, not every possible loss category or an authored calculation question.'],
 EF:['Expected percentage of asset value lost in one event.','Convert percent to a fraction for AV multiplication; not annual frequency or a currency amount. Percentage wording does not make the estimate certain.'],
 BCP:['Plan for sustaining critical business processes during disruption.','Broader business continuity differs from system-only disaster recovery or an analysis. Strategic wording is introductory; people, dependencies, testing and actual operation are not guaranteed.'],
 BIA:['Analysis identifies critical functions and business impacts of disruption.','An analysis informs priorities and recovery planning; it is not the continuity plan, a tested capability or a complete dependency/resource assessment in this short definition.'],
 COOP:['Planning or a plan supports mission-essential operations during emergencies.','Plan versus Planning is a wording difference, not a new family. Local crises/facility loss are examples; no universal restriction to local incidents, federal time/site mandate or equivalence to every BCP.'],
 MTBF:['Average operating interval between failures of a repairable system.','A population/model statistic, not each device guaranteed lifetime or repair duration; operating exposure and repeated-failure assumptions matter. No constant hazard or availability formula is established.'],
 MTTF:['Mean time until failure for non-repairable items.','Operating time/lifespan wording needs common units and a stated population/clock for comparison. Not every item fails at the mean; not repair duration, downtime target or universal aging model.'],
 MTTR:['Average repair or service-restoration duration, as introductory repair/recover vocabulary.','Repair work and verified service recovery can use different endpoints; any computed or compared mean requires a stated common clock and cohort. This bounded naming review excludes Respond and supplies no universal clock, achieved RTO or repair of the held glossary.'],
 ROI:['Compare investment benefits against costs.','Brief comparison vocabulary only; no particular net/gross/annualized formula, guaranteed return, monetized security benefit or investment recommendation is supplied. Time horizon and benefit/cost assumptions matter.'],
 RPO:['Acceptable data-loss window measured in time.','A recovery-data target, not repair duration, achieved backup frequency or guaranteed usable clean restore point. Actual copies and restore testing determine attained recovery.'],
 RTO:['Target duration for restoring a process or service.','A downtime/restoration target, not data-loss window, observed average MTTR or a service recovery guarantee. Endpoints and acceptable service must be defined.']
};
